      "content": {
        "block1": {
          "blockType": "hero",
          "title": "Help us explore premenstrual disorders across the menstrual cycle",
          "subtitle": "Join a King's College London research study using wearable and questionnaire data to better understand PMDD.<br /><br /><button style='font-size:1.05rem; padding:12px 28px; border-radius:999px;' variant='contained' href='PMDD-KCL/enrol'>Join Study</button>"
        },
        "block2": {
          "blockType": "markdown",
          "content": "<img src='https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RADAR-base/radar-self-enrolment-definitions/refs/heads/dev/projects/PMDD-KCL/resources/Image%201_Phone.jpeg' alt='Cycle Study hero image' style='width:90%; border-radius:24px; box-shadow:0 14px 32px rgba(20,20,20,0.14); object-fit:cover;'/>"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "blockType": "markdown",
      "noCard": true,
      "sx": {
        "width": "100%",
        "bgcolor": "#fff8f5",
        "color": "#2a2a2a",
        "& .MuiTypography-body1": {
          "fontSize": "1.15rem",
          "lineHeight": 1.75
        }
      },
      "title": "",
      "content": "<div style='max-width:980px; margin:0 auto; background:#ffffff; border-radius:20px; padding:2rem 2.2rem; box-shadow:0 10px 28px rgba(230,150,18,0.10); border:1px solid #f2c266;'><p style='margin-top:0;'>Premenstrual disorders, including <strong style='color:#950000;'>Premenstrual Syndrome (PMS)</strong> and <strong style='color:#950000;'>Premenstrual Dysphoric Disorder (PMDD)</strong>, can have severe effects on daily life.</p><ul style='margin:0.25rem 0 1rem 1.2rem;'><li style='margin-bottom:0.4rem;'><strong style='color:#e69612;'>1 in 3</strong> people who menstruate are clinically affected by PMS</li><li><strong style='color:#e69612;'>1 in 20</strong> people who menstruate are clinically affected by PMDD</li></ul><p>These conditions are characterised by physical and emotional symptoms that heighten during the <strong style='color:#950000;'>luteal phase</strong> (the time between ovulation and menstruation).</p><p style='margin-bottom:0;'>The Cycle Study aims to improve understanding of why premenstrual disorders occur and how to provide better support and treatment.</p></div>"
    },
    {
      "blockType": "column",
      "noCard": true,
      "sx": {
        "width": "100%",
        "paddingTop": "2.5rem",
        "paddingBottom": "2.5rem",
        "bgcolor": "#ffffff",
        "color": "#2a2a2a",
        "& .MuiTypography-h2": {
