      "content": {
        "block1": {
          "blockType": "markdown",
          "content": "<img src='https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RADAR-base/radar-self-enrolment-definitions/refs/heads/dev/projects/PMDD-KCL/resources/Image%203_Phone.jpeg' alt='Phone with study app' style='width:95%; border-radius:20px; box-shadow:0 12px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.12); object-fit:cover;'/>"
        },
        "block2": {
          "blockType": "markdown",
          "title": "About the Cycle Study",
          "content": "The Cycle Study, led by researchers at King's College London (KCL), explores how <strong style='color:#950000;'>PMDD fluctuates across the menstrual cycle</strong> and how it is influenced by environment, co-occurring conditions, and broader indicators of health.<br /><br />To do this, we combine questionnaire data with wearable device insights such as <strong style='color:#e69612;'>sleep</strong> and <strong style='color:#e69612;'>activity</strong> patterns."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "blockType": "markdown",
